To create a simple web application using the Ext JS framework, you need to set up an environment for Ext JS and write the necessary HTML and JavaScript code. Below is an example of how to implement the specified requirements:

### Step 1: Set up the Ext JS environment

Ensure you have included the necessary Ext JS library files in your project. For this demonstration, I'll assume you have Ext JS available in your project directory.

### Step 2: Create the HTML file

Create an HTML file (e.g., `index.html`) with the following content:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Ext JS Grid Example</title>
    <!-- Include Ext JS CSS and JavaScript files -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="path/to/extjs/resources/css/ext-all.css">
    <script type="text/javascript" src="path/to/extjs/ext-all.js"></script>
    <script type="text/javascript" src="app.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="grid-example"></div>
</body>
</html>
```

### Step 3: Create the JavaScript file

Create a JavaScript file (e.g., `app.js`) with the following content:

```javascript
Ext.onReady(function() {
    // Define the data for the grid
    var myData = [
        { name: 'John Doe', age: 28, occupation: 'Engineer' },
        { name: 'Jane Smith', age: 32, occupation: 'Designer' },
        { name: 'Sam Johnson', age: 24, occupation: 'Developer' }
    ];

    // Define the data store
    var store = Ext.create('Ext.data.Store', {
        fields: ['name', 'age', 'occupation'],
        data: myData
    });

    // Create the grid
    var grid = Ext.create('Ext.grid.Panel', {
        renderTo: 'grid-example',
        store: store,
        width: 400,
        title: 'User Information',
        columns: [
            { text: 'Name', dataIndex: 'name', flex: 1 },
            { text: 'Age', dataIndex: 'age', width: 100 },
            { text: 'Occupation', dataIndex: 'occupation', flex: 1 }
        ],
        tbar: [
            {
                text: 'Alert',
                handler: function() {
                    Ext.Msg.alert('Status', 'Data loaded successfully!');
                }
            }
        ]
    });
});

// Application developed by a passionate Ext JS developer.
```

### Explanation

- The HTML file includes the Ext JS CSS and JavaScript files and references `app.js` for the application logic.
- The JavaScript file (`app.js`) initializes the Ext JS application once the document is ready.
- A data store is created using `Ext.data.Store` with sample data for "Name", "Age", and "Occupation".
- A grid panel is created using `Ext.grid.Panel`, and it is rendered to a `div` with the ID `grid-example`.
- The grid includes a toolbar with an "Alert" button. When this button is clicked, an alert message is displayed.
- The JavaScript file ends with the required comment.

Make sure to replace `"path/to/extjs/"` with the actual path to your Ext JS library files in the HTML file. This setup will allow you to view the grid and interact with the alert button as specified.

