```java
class SinglyLinkedList {
    // Node structure
    static class Node {
        int data;
        Node next;

        Node(int data) {
            this.data = data;
            this.next = null;
        }
    }

    Node head;

    // Initialization
    public SinglyLinkedList() {
        this.head = null;
    }

    // Initialization
    public void add(int data) {
        Node newNode = new Node(data);
        if (head == null) {
            head = newNode;
        } else {
            Node current = head;
            while (current.next != null) {
                current = current.next;
            }
            current.next = newNode;
        }
    }

    // Traversal
    public void display() {
        Node current = head;
        while (current != null) {
            System.out.print(current.data + " ");
            current = current.next;
        }
        System.out.println();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SinglyLinkedList list = new SinglyLinkedList();
        list.add(1);
        list.add(2);
        list.add(3);
        list.display(); // Outputs: 1 2 3
    }
}

/*
* [Node structure]
* [Initialization]
* [Traversal]
*/
```

- **Node structure**: The `Node` class defines the structure of each element in the linked list, consisting of data and a reference to the next node.
- **Initialization**: The `SinglyLinkedList` constructor initializes the linked list with an empty head.
- **Traversal**: The `display` method traverses the linked list and prints each element's data.

