A study led by Finkel et al. explored how forgiveness affects trust and commitment in romantic relationships. The researchers used a combination of surveys and experimental methods to assess the interplay between these factors. Their findings indicated that forgiveness could strengthen trust and commitment, especially when the offending partner demonstrated genuine remorse and a commitment to change. The study emphasized that forgiveness is not a one-time act but a process that involves rebuilding trust and fostering a renewed sense of commitment. This research suggests that forgiveness can lead to a deeper, more resilient bond between partners when coupled with positive behavioral changes.

