===

{{Future Challenges and Opportunities}}

As metropolitan areas continue to grow, urban parks face both challenges and opportunities in adapting to the needs of their communities. Climate change poses significant threats, with extreme weather events and rising temperatures impacting park ecosystems. Consequently, there is a pressing need for sustainable park management practices that emphasize biodiversity and resilience. On the other hand, the push for more green spaces presents an opportunity to tackle urban issues such as pollution and urban heat islands. Future urban parks are likely to integrate innovative technologies, such as smart irrigation systems and renewable energy sources, to enhance their functionality and sustainability. Additionally, there is an increasing emphasis on community participation in park planning and development, ensuring that these spaces reflect the diverse needs of urban populations. As cities continue to evolve, so too will the role of urban parks, remaining vital to the health and well-being of their inhabitants.

