```matlab
% MATLAB Script: Damped Harmonic Oscillator Simulation

% Define customizable parameters
MASS = 1.0; % Mass of the oscillator in kg
DAMPING_COEFFICIENT = 0.1; % Damping coefficient
SPRING_CONSTANT = 5.0; % Spring constant in N/m

% Define time parameters
TIME_STEP = 0.01; % Time step for the simulation
TOTAL_TIME = 10; % Total simulation time in seconds

% Calculate derived parameters
omega_n = sqrt(SPRING_CONSTANT / MASS); % Natural frequency
zeta = DAMPING_COEFFICIENT / (2 * sqrt(MASS * SPRING_CONSTANT)); % Damping ratio

% Time vector
t = 0:TIME_STEP:TOTAL_TIME;

% Initial conditions
x0 = 1.0; % Initial displacement
v0 = 0.0; % Initial velocity

% Preallocate arrays for displacement and velocity
x = zeros(size(t));
v = zeros(size(t));

% Assign initial conditions
x(1) = x0;
v(1) = v0;

% Simulate the damped harmonic oscillator
for i = 1:length(t)-1
    % Acceleration using the equation of motion
    a = -(2 * zeta * omega_n * v(i)) - (omega_n^2 * x(i));

    % Update velocity and displacement using Euler's method
    v(i+1) = v(i) + a * TIME_STEP;
    x(i+1) = x(i) + v(i) * TIME_STEP;
end

% Plot the results
figure;
plot(t x 'LineWidth' 2);
xlabel('Time (s)');
ylabel('Displacement (m)');
title('Damped Harmonic Oscillator');
grid on;
```

This script models the vibration of a damped harmonic oscillator with placeholders for `MASS` `DAMPING_COEFFICIENT` and `SPRING_CONSTANT` allowing easy modification of these parameters.

